# Module PrestaShop compatibility and Marketplace readiness

Module code must run on PrestaShop **1.7.x, 8.x, and 9.x** unless the product scope says otherwise. PHP syntax limits live in `module-php.mdc`.

- Do **not** add new PrestaShop 1.6-only code paths.
- Existing 1.6 fallbacks may stay untouched; do not extend them.
- `config.xml` `ps_versions_compliancy` min should be `1.7.0.0` for new work.
- New Marketplace submissions must support the latest major PrestaShop version. As of the Marketplace docs, this means **9.x**.
- For Marketplace-targeted modules, keep the module technical name stable across ZIP versions.

Reference docs:
- https://docs.cloud.prestashop.com/
- https://docs.cloud.prestashop.com/2-technical-development-standards/
- https://docs.cloud.prestashop.com/3-content-and-marketing-standards/
- https://docs.cloud.prestashop.com/4-quality-standards-and-verified-plus/

## Entrypoint guard

Every PHP file must include the PrestaShop context guard near the top:

```php
if (!defined('_PS_VERSION_')) {
    exit;
}
```

Every directory should contain an `index.php` directory-protection file. The module root should include `.htaccess` protection when packaged for Marketplace distribution.

## Core API (1.7+ baseline)

```php
$row = Db::getInstance()->getRow('SELECT ...');
$val = Db::getInstance()->getValue('SELECT ...');
Db::getInstance()->execute('INSERT ...');

Configuration::get('KEY');
Configuration::updateValue('KEY', $value);

$ctx = Context::getContext();
```

SQL escaping: `module-sql.mdc`. Request validation: `module-input.mdc`.

Configuration keys must be namespaced with the module prefix, for example `MYMODULE_API_KEY`, never generic names like `API_KEY` or `ENABLED`.

## Version-gated features

Branch when behaviour differs across 1.7 / 8 / 9:

```php
if (version_compare(_PS_VERSION_, '9.0.0', '>=')) {
    // PS 9 path
} elseif (version_compare(_PS_VERSION_, '8.0.0', '>=')) {
    // PS 8 path (Symfony services, new admin patterns, …)
} else {
    // PS 1.7 path
}
```

- Never `require` / `use` a class that exists only in PS 8+ at top level — load inside the guard.
- Admin hooks, grid definitions, and container access differ by major — follow patterns already used in the same module file.
- Declare precise compatibility in the main module constructor. Do not use `_PS_VERSION_` as the max value.

```php
$this->ps_versions_compliancy = [
    'min' => '1.7.0.0',
    'max' => '9.99.99',
];
```

If a Marketplace product intentionally targets only PS 8/9, use the product's declared minimum version instead of the project default above.

## Templates & assets

- Module admin UI: follow the module's existing Smarty/Twig mix; do not assume Twig in PS 1.7.
- BO CSS/JS: test on both legacy BO (1.7) and new theme (8+) when touching shared assets.
- Load BO assets only where needed — see `module-security.mdc`.

Smarty variables must be escaped unless the value is trusted HTML and explicitly reviewed:

```smarty
{$user_content|escape:'htmlall':'UTF-8'}
{$url_param|escape:'url'}
```

Use `nofilter` only for controlled hook output or already-sanitised module HTML.

## Marketplace technical rules

Before considering a module Marketplace-ready:

- Do not modify PrestaShop core files, core database tables, or other modules.
- Prefer hooks over overrides. If an override is unavoidable, document why no hook can satisfy the requirement.
- The module must produce zero errors, warnings, or notices with debug mode enabled.
- All code, comments, and default text must be in English.
- For SQL, validation, uploads, tokens, and logging, follow `module-sql.mdc`, `module-input.mdc`, `module-security.mdc`, and `module-logging.mdc`.
- Do not use `eval`, `serialize` / `unserialize` for user-controlled data, or unrestricted `file_get_contents`, `include`, or path operations.
- Use JSON for structured data storage/interchange and encode safely, for example `JSON_HEX_TAG | JSON_HEX_AMP`.
- Hooks must be lightweight and exit early when the current controller/page is irrelevant.

## Marketplace package and product page

When preparing or reviewing a Marketplace release:

- Package the standard module structure: `config.xml`, main module PHP file, protected directories, `views/`, `controllers/`, optional documented `override/`, `docs/`, and root `.htaccess`.
- Product name should follow `[Primary Function]: [Brief Explanation]`, avoid "PrestaShop", "Module", version numbers, unlicensed brand names, and unsupported superlatives.
- Short description is max 250 characters and should explain merchant value, not only technical implementation.
- Document at least 3 distinct, measurable features and clear merchant/customer benefits.
- Product icon must be exactly 256x256 JPG/PNG and must not use PrestaShop branding or unlicensed external logos.
- Provide at least 3 screenshots per supported language, minimum 1000x1000, with realistic data and no contact information or watermarks.
- User guide must be PDF, English mandatory, named like `readme_en.pdf`, and cover compatibility, PHP requirements, installation, configuration, features, troubleshooting, and FAQ.
- Demo credentials, when provided, should use the Marketplace convention: `[email protected]` / `demodemo`, with restricted back-office permissions and regular reset.

## Verified+ readiness

To keep a module eligible for Verified+ style review, preserve:

- Clean PrestaShop Validator scan.
- No known security vulnerabilities.
- Minimal, justified overrides only.
- Error-free execution on the supported PHP versions for each supported PrestaShop major.
- Compatibility with at least the 2 latest PrestaShop major versions when the product claims broad support.
- No debug-mode errors across supported versions.
